<title>USA: U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - Nov 6.</title>
<headline>U.S. HEADLINE STOCKS - Issues to Watch - Nov 6.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Stocks to watch this morning:</p>
<p>-- CSX raised the cash portion of its bid for Conrail to $110 per share. Conrail shares closed off 1-3/8 at 92-1/4 on Tuesday.</p>
<p>-- Texas Instruments wants to sell off its defense electronics holdings, worth $2 billion or more, and McDonnell Douglas Corp is one of the interested buyers, according to the Wall Street Journal.</p>
<p>Texas Instruments shares closed at 49.  </p>
<p>hostile bid for 65 percent of Loctite Corp at $57.75 a share. Loctite shares closed at 57-5/8.</p>
<p>-- Bennett Lebow is proposing his own slate of nominees to RJR Nabisco's board. RJR shares closed at 29-1/8.</p>
<p>-- General Motors said it reached a tentative agreement to end to a strike at its Janesville, Wis., plant. GM shares closed at 55-7/8.</p>
<p>-- Ingram Micro posted third quarter earnings of $0.22 a share, compared to $0.17 in the year-ago period. Shares closed at 21-3/4.  </p>
<p>-- Cisco reported earnings of $0.26 a share, above estimates, but traded slightly lower after hours. Shares closed at 61-3/4.</p>
